<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Manius Curius Dentatus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 270 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century-bce">3rd century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Manius Curius Dentatus was a Roman general and statesman of plebeian origin. As consul in 290 BCE he ended the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/third-samnite-war">Third Samnite War</a> and conquered the Sabines, and in 275 BCE he defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pyrrhus-of-epirus">Pyrrhus of Epirus</a> near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benevento">Beneventum</a>. He also began the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aniene">Anio</a> Vetus aqueduct and was remembered by later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Romans</a> as a model of frugal, incorruptible virtue.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/manius-curius-dentatus.jpg" alt="Manius Curius Dentatus" width="320" height="392" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jacopo Amigoni · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dentatus.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
